---
import Contact from '../components/Contact.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// The site's privacy notice, which UK data protection law asks for because the enquiry form collects names and contact
// details. It also covers cookies: the site sets none of its own, and hCaptcha's security cookie needs no consent, so
// there's no cookie banner. Update `updated` whenever the wording changes, and this page whenever a service that
// handles visitors' details (the form, the "I am human" check, email or hosting) is added or changed.
const updated = '22 October 2026';
const email = 'hello@thequietcalligrapher.com';

const linkClass =
  'underline decoration-gold-500 decoration-1 underline-offset-[0.25em] hover:text-gold-700 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-gold-700';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy & Cookies"
  description="How The Quiet Calligrapher uses the details you send through the enquiry form, and the cookies this website does and doesn’t use."
>
  <article class="bg-cream-100 px-gutter py-20 text-ink sm:py-24 lg:py-28">
    <div
      class="mx-auto max-w-[40rem] text-lg leading-[1.65] font-medium text-pretty text-ink/80 lg:text-[1.1875rem] [&_h2]:mt-12 [&_h2]:text-[1.75rem] [&_h2]:leading-tight [&_h2]:text-ink lg:[&_h2]:text-[2rem] [&_h2+*]:mt-4 [&_p+p]:mt-5"
    >
      <h1 class="text-[2.25rem] leading-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl lg:text-[3.5rem]">Privacy &amp; Cookies</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-gold-700 uppercase">Last updated {updated}</p>
      <span class="mt-5 mb-8 block h-px w-16 bg-gold-500" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <p>
        This page explains what happens to the details you share with The Quiet Calligrapher, and the cookies this website
        does and doesn’t use.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is responsible for your details</h2>
      <p>
        The Quiet Calligrapher, run by Aliya in Birmingham, is responsible for the personal details you send (“we” and
        “us” below). You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${email}`} class={linkClass}>{email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        When you send an enquiry through this website, we receive your name, your email address, your phone number if you
        give it, the service you choose and your message. If you email us directly, we receive your email address and
        whatever your email contains.
      </p>
      <p>We don’t ask for anything else, and this website doesn’t follow you as you browse it.</p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>
        We use your details only to reply to your enquiry and, if you go ahead, to arrange and provide what you’ve asked
        for. We never sell them, and we won’t send you marketing unless you ask us to.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do this because you’ve asked us to (so we can take the steps you’ve requested before agreeing any work), and
        because we have a legitimate interest in replying to people who contact us.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else handles it</h2>
      <p>A few services handle your details for us:</p>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-[0.8em] h-px w-3 shrink-0 bg-gold-500" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>
            <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Web3Forms</strong> (Web3Creative, India) delivers the enquiry form to our
            inbox. It checks enquiries for spam, using CleanTalk and Akismet, and keeps a copy for up to three
            years.{' '}
            <a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy" class={linkClass}>Its privacy policy</a>
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-[0.8em] h-px w-3 shrink-0 bg-gold-500" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>
            <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">hCaptcha</strong> (Intuition Machines, Inc., USA) runs the “I am human”
            check on the form. To tell people from bots, it looks at how you use the page, such as mouse movements, taps
            and key presses, and at your IP address, browser and device.{' '}
            <a href="https://www.hcaptcha.com/privacy" class={linkClass}>Its privacy policy</a>
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-[0.8em] h-px w-3 shrink-0 bg-gold-500" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">IONOS</strong> hosts our email.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-[0.8em] h-px w-3 shrink-0 bg-gold-500" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>
            <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Vercel</strong> (Vercel Inc., USA) hosts this website. Like any web host,
            it records visitors’ IP addresses to deliver pages and keep the site secure.{' '}
            <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" class={linkClass}>Its privacy policy</a>
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-5">
        Some of these services handle your details outside the UK. Their privacy policies explain how they protect them
        when they do.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep your enquiry for as long as we need it to reply and, if you book, to provide your order or lessons. After
        that we delete it, apart from any records the law requires us to keep, such as for tax.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask for a copy of the details we hold about you, and ask us to correct them, delete them or stop using
        them. Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`} class={linkClass}>{email}</a> and we’ll reply within a month.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you’re unhappy with how we’ve handled your details, you can complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office
        at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" class={linkClass}>ico.org.uk</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This website doesn’t set any cookies of its own, and it doesn’t use analytics, advertising or social media
        trackers.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you scroll down to the enquiry form, hCaptcha’s “I am human” check loads. hCaptcha and Cloudflare, which
        protects it, may then set security cookies such as <code class="font-sans text-base">__cf_bm</code>, which lasts
        30 minutes and helps tell people from bots. These cookies are strictly necessary to protect the form from spam,
        so they don’t need your consent. Some browsers, such as Safari, block them anyway.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Instagram, TikTok and Etsy links take you to those websites, which have their own privacy and cookie
        policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
      <p>If we change this page, we’ll update the date at the top.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
  <Contact />
</Layout>
